# ── MARK LV — what never belongs in the repository ──────────────────────────
# Everything listed here is created by the app on first run. A fresh clone with
# none of it present boots straight to the setup screen, which is the intended
# first experience — so nothing here needs to be committed, and some of it must
# never be.

# ── Secrets. Committing any of these publishes them. ──────────────────────────
# NOTE: git has no inline comments — '#' only starts a comment at line start, so
# each explanation lives on its own line and every pattern stays bare.
config/api_keys.json
# ^ your Gemini API key, plus per-plugin credentials
config/certs/
# ^ the dashboard's TLS private key and certificate
config/whatsapp_web/
# ^ a LINKED WhatsApp session — committing it hands somebody your WhatsApp
#   account, not just a key
**/token*.json
# ^ OAuth token files: Google (Gmail / Calendar plugins) and Spotify
#   (config/spotify_token.json — the Web API refresh token, mode 0600)
**/client_secret*.json
# ^ Google OAuth client secrets
site_credentials*.json
# ^ browser-agent login store (the real store lives outside the repo in
#   ~/.local/share/jarvis-browser-profile/)
!scripts/site_credentials.template.json
# ^ ...but the schema template is safe (only an _example_ entry) and belongs
#   in the repo
*credentials*.json
# ^ any credential blobs anywhere in the tree
!scripts/site_credentials.template.json
# ^ re-un-ignored after the wildcard above: the schema template (only an
#   _example_ entry, no secrets) is documentation and belongs in the repo
.env
.env.*
# ^ the REAL, machine-local env file with live secrets — never commit it.
# But the *documented* example (no secrets, only `your_key_here` placeholders)
# IS meant to be shared so new installs know what to set.
!.env.example

# ── Personal data the assistant accumulates about you ─────────────────────────
memory/long_term.json
memory/*.db
memory/conversations/
# ^ the verbatim conversation journal
memory/_last_spoken_session
memory/_evolution_state.json

# ── Python build noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ── Virtual environments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
.venv-tradingagents/

# Secrets that once got committed: live API keys, device pairing tokens.
config/api_keys.json.bak*
config/dashboard_devices.json
env/
ENV/

# ── Deb-extracted system libs (libxcb-cursor0 workaround; see run.sh) ─────────
.system-libs/

# ── Editors and operating systems ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Runtime output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
downloads/
screenshots/
memory/trading/train_cache/
# ^ regenerable 5y OHLCV disk cache for ML training — refetches when stale
memory/browser_agent/runs.jsonl
memory/scientific/jobs/
memory/scientific/reports/
memory/scientific/mpl_cache/
memory/scientific/skills_index.json
memory/scientific/runs.jsonl
# ^ science agent runtime: job dirs, generated reports, matplotlib cache, the
#   metadata index (regenerable). registry.json and config.json stay tracked.
memory/browser_agent/downloads/
memory/browser_agent/failures/
# ^ browser agent run log + files the browser downloaded + kept artifacts for
#   failed runs (page text/screenshots). config.json stays tracked.
models/
# ^ local GGUF models (core/llm_local.py) — ~1.9 GB binaries, refetchable from HF

# ── RAG knowledge base ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Personal documents + vectors + audit — private to this machine.
knowledge/

# ── Portable mode build artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────
# scripts/build_portable.py output (~2-4 GB runtime + deps) and the writable
# jarvis-home/ a launcher run creates (config, memories, journal). The build
# output is meant to be copied onto the stick, the home is personal data.
jarvis-portable-build/
jarvis-portable/
jarvis-home/

# ── Regenerable media ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# core/media_prep.py converts AV1 (and anything else the bundled Qt FFmpeg
# cannot decode) to H.264 here. Derived from a file the user already has, so it
# must never be committed; deleting it only costs one conversion.
cache/

# ── Secret backups ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
config/*.backup
config/*.bak*
config/*.key
config/*.crt
config/*.pem

# ── Build artifacts and developer tools ───────────────────────────────────
himalaya/target/
.agents/
node_modules/

# ── User data and generated output ────────────────────────────────────────
uploads/
desk_journal/
*.db
*.db-journal

# ── Memory: keep only top-level Python source files ───────────────────────
memory/*
!memory/*.py

# ── Personal source snapshots ──────────────────────────────────────────────
backup/
